        "Projects: parts, plates and files with pictures from the slicer, the plan and the result for each part with −/+ buttons, deadlines, archive, search and sorting. Project folders are named after the project; files from a USB stick are copied into the program storage and stay available after the stick is removed.",
        "Projects: “Print whole project” — the program counts how many parts are left and which plates to print how many times, shows surplus parts, checks the material source (spool, slot, material, colour — close shades are told apart the way a person sees them) and the “Plate cleared” confirmation. Every start is confirmed by a person; nothing starts by itself.",
        "Tasks: a list of files with plan and result, search, filters, grouping by project, trouble marks (“file missing”, “no suitable printer”), a progress bar, a note on the second line and a large preview on hover. Syncing a task with a project is turned on with a switch; the result grows with every successful print, including beyond the plan.",
